4. CASE TEXT -- THE ONLY CASE IN THIS CAMPAIGN WITH REAL AUTHORED STEPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
AWPTCM T43849 "IPv4_ARP - Local Proxy ARP: Functionality".
ck.db exact-title match: **AWP-4357 / internal_id 25060**, unique, `steps_text` 517 chars.
Quoted verbatim:

  > Configure DUT and BackupSW / Connect both SW via VLAN 23 / Configure DUT as follows:
  > interface VLAN23, iP address 23.1.1.1/24, ip local-proxy-arp / Configure BackupSW as follows:
  > interface VLAN23, ip address 23.1.1.2/16 / From BackupSW, ping 23.1.1.3 / Expect ping to
  > fail, but with ARP using DUT MAC address. DUT responds to ARPs on an interface for other IP
  > hosts that would be on the same interface. This is a "one armed router" situation eg when
  > private vlans are configured. DUT MAC address will be saved on BackupSW ARP table

EXPECTED RESULT, as authored: the ping FAILS, and BackupSW's ARP table holds the DUT's MAC for
23.1.1.3.  The deliberate /24-vs-/16 mask mismatch is the mechanism: with 23.1.1.2/16, BackupSW
believes 23.1.1.3 is on-link and ARPs for it instead of routing to it.

**The authored steps are followed as written** (step 3 below), on real hardware, with swi_b as
BackupSW.  They are then supplemented -- not replaced -- by crafted-frame legs (step 2), because
the authored check "ARP using DUT MAC address" is read off swi_b's ARP table, and the queue
requires the ARP exchange itself to be measured on the wire (STANDING-ORDERS Section 7; the
queue: "Proxy ARP is an ARP-level question ... A ping would hide the whole mechanism").
Both limbs are reported.  Extra limbs: a no-route control, an out-of-subnet control that probes
the /16 boundary, removal, and reboot persistence (memory `satisfactory-level-of-testing`).

Also grounded in: X960 platform support TPS row 24 "Local Proxy-ARP" (priority 1, "Yes", note
column empty); `ip_feature_overview_guide.pdf` Local Proxy ARP, p9; and the DUT's own CLI:
  awplus(config-if)# ip local-proxy-arp ?
    <cr>
`ip limited-local-proxy-arp` also exists on this build (seen at triage).  It is a DIFFERENT
feature and is NOT exercised here; recorded as present, not tested.


