PROBLEM 1 -- RSTP BLOCKED THE PARTNER LINK (queue RISK-4, and the per-VLAN remedy does not work).

  Immediately after the VLAN 23 setup:
    awplus# show spanning-tree brief
    Default: Root Path Cost 20000 - Root Port 5002 -  Bridge Priority 32768
    Default: Root Id 8000:0000cd423029          <- swi_b is the root bridge
    Default: Bridge Id 8000:e01aead47043
    port1.0.2       8000:0000cd423029    838a   Rootport     Forwarding   (to swi_b)
    port1.0.4       8000:889d98df2602    838c   Alternate    Discarding   (to swi_a)
    port1.0.10      8000:e01aead47043    8392   Designated   Forwarding   (host eth3)
    port1.0.14      8000:889d98df2602    8396   Alternate    Discarding   (to swi_a)
    port1.0.16      8000:0000cd423029    8398   Alternate    Discarding   <- THE CASE'S LINK

  The leg this case depends on was Discarding.  Measuring across it would have produced zero
  replies at swi_b, which is indistinguishable from the feature not working -- a false FAIL on
  the one case in this campaign that has authored steps.

  The triage's RISK-4 remedy ("give every routed leg its own VLAN") does NOT apply: both
  devices run `spanning-tree mode rstp`, a SINGLE instance, not MSTP or PVST.  Under
  single-instance RSTP a Discarding port is blocked for every VLAN, so moving the leg into
  VLAN 23 cannot unblock it.

  RESOLUTION CHOSEN: take the redundant link out of the topology for the duration of the case,
  on the DUT side only, changing no partner configuration:
    awplus(config)# interface port1.0.2
    awplus(config-if)# shutdown
  port1.0.2 was the DUT's root port to swi_b; with it down, the only remaining DUT<->swi_b path
  is port1.0.16, which RSTP promotes.  One port, DUT-side, fully reversible.  Rejected
  alternatives: changing `spanning-tree mode` (silently drops any `no spanning-tree <mode>
  enable` -- memory `stp-mode-change-reenables-spanning-tree`); touching swi_b's `sa1` (RISK-2);
  re-costing ports on swi_b (two partner config changes instead of one DUT change).

  After the shutdown, 15 s for RSTP to converge:
    awplus# show spanning-tree brief
    Default: Root Path Cost 20000 - Root Port 5016
    port1.0.2       8000:e01aead47043    838a   Disabled     Discarding
