7. PROBLEM 2 -- `no interface vlanN` IS REFUSED; DELETING THE VLAN IS WHAT REMOVES THE SVI
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
At teardown, on BOTH devices:

  awplus(config)# no interface vlan23
  % Removal of interface not allowed

Tried, and still refused, after:
  (a) removing the SVI's address first (`interface vlan23 / no ip address`) -- which is the
      order the 2026-10-15 session handover's recipe gives; and then additionally
  (b) moving EVERY member port out of VLAN 23 first (port1.0.10 -> vlan 10,
      port1.0.16 -> vlan 1), confirmed with `show vlan brief`:
        23      VLAN0023         STATIC  ACTIVE          <- no ports listed

What works is deleting the VLAN from the database, which takes the SVI with it:

  awplus(config)# vlan database
  awplus(config-vlan)# no vlan 23
  awplus(config-vlan)# exit
  awplus# show vlan brief                 -> no VLAN 23 row
  awplus# show running-config interface vlan23   -> empty
  awplus# show ip interface brief         -> vlan10 and vlan48 only

=> CORRECTION TO THE RECIPE IN THE 2026-10-15 HANDOVER: removing the address is not sufficient
   on this build, and neither is emptying the VLAN of ports.  The reliable teardown order is
   **ports out of the VLAN -> `vlan database` / `no vlan N`**, and `no interface vlanN` is not
   needed at all.  This matters for groups B/C/D, whose restore block uses `no interface vlanN`.

   It also cost this case a real teardown bug, recorded honestly in section 8: `cfg.py` stops at
   the first `% ` line, so the `% Removal of interface not allowed` ABORTED THE REST OF THE
   TEARDOWN BATCH -- including the `no shutdown` on port1.0.2 -- twice.  The residue was caught
   only by diffing, which is why the diff is not optional.


